# BUG-326 regression pin: sys.exit() with a value outside 0..255 SEGFAULTED the program
# (exit 139) and lost everything buffered on stdout. Measured before the fix: 0/1/2/255
# were fine, -1 and 256 both crashed with the preceding print() never appearing.
#
# THE FIXTURE EXITS 0 ON PURPOSE, and that is what makes it usable as a smoke_run. 256
# truncates to 0 the way C's exit() does, so this exercises the crashing path -- a value
# outside u8 -- while still terminating cleanly enough for the harness to check output.
# If the bug returns, this segfaults, prints nothing, and smoke fails on the missing
# marker rather than on an exit code the harness would have to special-case.
#
# The negative direction (-1 -> 255) cannot be pinned the same way without the harness
# treating a non-zero exit as failure; it is covered by tools/ checks instead.

def main()
    print("bug326: OK")
    sys.exit(256)
